        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: राहत",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "राहत — rāhat — \"relief\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सरकार ने गाँव में राहत भेजी। sarkār ne gā̃v meṁ rāhat bhejī. The government sent relief to the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "राहत (rāhat) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic rāḥa, \"rest, ease\". It is both the feeling of relief and the food and blankets sent after a disaster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
